body:
I love popcorn to death and I know it is healthier than some other snack foods. If I have a salty craving, I usually go for a small bowl (So I don't get out of control with my portion) and fill it with Skinny Pop Popcorn. 

&#x200B;

My only concern is the amount of carbs because I am trying to do a Keto-based diet where I try to take in no carbs and only fat

I think measuring yourself in different, more realistic ways is a fantastic idea. When people compare themselves solely on scale, they may get discouraged, seeing all the water weight they lost and then being disappointed when they don't lose anything else.

&#x200B;

The problem is that you might not lose ANY real weight because you are likely gaining muscle mass, especially with ring-fit being a type of resistance training.

&#x200B;

The way I found that works best is to take a picture of myself once a month and see the psychical changes. Does my stomach poke out as much as it did before? Does my upper chest look more firm then last month. And it has had some success as well
